// Engine test (session 2): story voice, pronouns and names, origin variants,
// the decision log and journal, and carrying a save into a second book. Not part of the story.
@chapter etb1
@title Engine Test: Voices, Names, Variants
@book engine-test-b
@version 1

# start
## Who you are
?if quick_start
  This book began with a quick start.
?end
?if et.door == "left" or et.door == "right"
  Last book you took the {et.door} door.
?else
  This test was started without the first engine test.
?end
---
$ _h = hunger
You are {name}, {alias} to the city, of the {surname} family.
{They} {are} ready. {They} wait{s} at the gate, {their} hand on the latch.
Your {pg("spouse", "husband", "wife", "spouse")}, {spouse.name}, watches {them}. {spouse.They} {spouse.are} worried.
Right now {voice("hunger")}, and {voice("humanity")}.
[roman] As a citizen, you know these streets.
[gaul briton] Rome still feels like a conqueror's city to you.
[not roman gaul briton] You came to Rome from far away.
[gladiator] Your arena scar itches.
---
~> homeland [origin]
$ hunger += 50
Now {voice("hunger")}. In a word: {voice("hunger", "short")}.
?if band("hunger") == "hungry" or band("hunger") == "starving" or band("hunger") == "ravenous"
  The hunger band check works.
?end
$ hunger = _h
$ do journal("The engine test reached its second book.", "Engine Test")
* Greet the stranger in Brittonic ?if [briton]
  $ standing += 5
  The stranger answers you gladly.
* Nod and move on
  You nod and move on.
:end_choice
---
=> endbook

# homeland
You think of home, wherever it was.
<~

# homeland_roman
You think of the Seven Hills.
<~

# homeland_briton
You think of grey seas and the island's mists.
<~
